import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const h=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 274 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Strange Beasts and Foreign Races' Situation: The 99% Forgotten by Universal Benefit","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 274 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Strange Beasts and Foreign Races' Situation: The 99% Forgotten by Universal Benefit","no":274,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Strange Beasts","Foreign Races","Universal-Benefit Forgotten","99%","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["50-Myriad Races Genealogy Overview","52-Foreign-Race Classification and Symbiosis","53-Strange-Life Recognition Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0274_模块2-唐罗-异兽与异族处境.md","filePath":"en/0274_模块2-唐罗-异兽与异族处境.md"}`),s={name:"en/0274_模块2-唐罗-异兽与异族处境.md"};function o(r,e,l,u,g,d){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-274-tang-luo-decomposition-strange-beasts-and-foreign-races-situation-the-99-forgotten-by-universal-benefit" tabindex="-1">Entry 274 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Strange Beasts and Foreign Races&#39; Situation: The 99% Forgotten by Universal Benefit <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-274-tang-luo-decomposition-strange-beasts-and-foreign-races-situation-the-99-forgotten-by-universal-benefit" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 274 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Strange Beasts and Foreign Races&#39; Situation: The 99% Forgotten by Universal Benefit&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 24)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-universal-benefit-is-named-all-beings-but-the-list-has-only-humanity" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Universal benefit is named &quot;all beings,&quot; but the list has only humanity <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-universal-benefit-is-named-all-beings-but-the-list-has-only-humanity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Universal benefit is named &quot;all beings,&quot; but the list has only humanity&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires 99% full coverage of Myriad Races. On Tang Luo&#39;s universal-benefit list, strange beasts, foreign races, plant spirits, planet consciousness are all absent. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, specifically making a situation report for &quot;the forgotten 99%.&quot; Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong>. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The forgotten ones&#39; energy-level waste:</p><ul><li><strong>Strange-beast talent idled</strong>: demon beasts that can open sentience, rare insects that can breathe spiritual qi, their cultivation talent is not recognized in the Tang-Luo system. Human cultivators meeting them, first reaction is &quot;hunt demon for elixir&quot;</li><li><strong>Foreign-race civilizations suppressed</strong>: mountain foreign races, sea-floor clans, starry sky remnants originally had their own cultivation traditions. Tang Luo&#39;s universal benefit did not dialogue with them, but default-classified them as &quot;to be civilized / to be suppressed&quot;</li><li><strong>Planet consciousness voiceless</strong>: mountain-river wills, continental spirit consciousness are the world&#39;s own life. In the Tang-Luo system they are not even &quot;characters,&quot; only background boards</li></ul><p>Energy-level waste: <strong>expelling 99% of sentient beings from &quot;all beings&quot; is equivalent to cutting civilization&#39;s talent pool, knowledge base, ecological foundation all by 90%.</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Human-demon war normalized</strong>: because strange beasts have no upward channel, they can only take preying on human resources as survival strategy. War is structurally inevitable</li><li><strong>Ecological destruction</strong>: humanity for resources suppresses demon beasts, destroys spirit veins, long-term damages world ecology. After a hundred years spirit veins deplete, humanity itself declines with it</li><li><strong>Knowledge isolation</strong>: human methods lose collision with foreign-race methods, stagnate after a hundred years</li></ol><p>Regression form: the stronger humanity is, the more barren the world; the more barren the world, the more humanity cannot get stronger.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Hunting demons is predation</strong>: treating strange beasts as &quot;elixir sources&quot; is treating sentient life as resources. This is the most straightforward predation</li><li><strong>Othering is predation</strong>: strange beasts, foreign races in the Tang-Luo system are not &quot;we,&quot; but &quot;they.&quot; After othering, preying on them is no longer a moral issue</li><li><strong>Silence is predation</strong>: Tang Luo never legislated for them, never spoke for them. Silence itself is acquiescence — acquiescing to humanity continuing to prey</li></ul><p>By the Gu Chensha / Tang Luo judgment table standard: Tang Luo = <strong>enlightened predator</strong>, his predation radius extends to the entire non-human world. His good toward humanity is real, but this good does not cross species.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tang-Luo Forgets 99%</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Covers 99%</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Strange beasts = elixirs</td><td>Strange beasts opening sentience included in Myriad Races genealogy, cultivated by talent</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign races = to be suppressed</td><td>Foreign-Race Classification and Symbiosis: dialogue, treaty, co-governance</td></tr><tr><td>Planet consciousness = background board</td><td>Strange-Life Recognition Standards: planet consciousness as independent contracting party</td></tr><tr><td>Human-demon war</td><td>Myriad Races republicanism, ecological reconciliation written into constitution</td></tr><tr><td>Resources by race</td><td>Resources by contribution, race no longer the distribution unit</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: turn &quot;99%&quot; from list silence into institutional seats.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Tang-Luo world, marking Myriad Races distribution and human-demon war parameters</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Group A maintains status quo; Group B injects Myriad Races republicanism</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: war frequency within a hundred years, spirit-vein health, Myriad Races overall energy</li><li><strong>Review expectation</strong>: Group B war frequency drops 90%, spirit-vein health actually rises — proving symbiosis is more &quot;cost-effective&quot; than predation</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-high</strong>. Human-demon opposition is its world-view底色</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong>. Long-form late if it needs &quot;demon allies&quot; against new enemies, the early &quot;non-human is demon&quot; setting is torn by plot; or to create climaxes, temporarily let some demon beast &quot;suddenly shapeshift, suddenly reasons&quot;</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: 99% of sentient beings idled</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: hunting demons = elixir-style predation, othering rationalizes predation</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s universal-benefit list missed 90%</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: this entry is a direct call of the Myriad Races 99% coverage axiom</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: without covering Myriad Races, cross-plane cooperation cannot be discussed</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="supplementary-discussion-rights-return-of-the-forgotten" tabindex="-1">Supplementary Discussion: Rights Return of the Forgotten <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplementary-discussion-rights-return-of-the-forgotten" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplementary Discussion: Rights Return of the Forgotten&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Strange beasts and foreign races being forgotten by universal benefit in the Tang-Luo system is not because Tang Luo is evil-hearted, but because the bestowal system&#39;s coverage radius is naturally finite. Heng Yuan Zhou through the Alaya Network extends Myriad Races coverage from humanity to 99% of sentient genealogies. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s Myriad Races republicanism is not charity, but the law-first axiom&#39;s requirement — laws are equally effective for all beings, no reason to protect only humanity. The universal equal infinite law provides the origin basis for strange beasts&#39; and foreign races&#39; rights: they inherently possess basic infinite power, evolution rights are inalienable.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Tang Luo&#39;s universal benefit is named &quot;all beings,&quot; but the list has only humanity. The forgotten 99% are not numbers, they are nine lives, nine civilizations, nine talents. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judgment: a universal benefit not covering 99% is only one race&#39;s welfare — and one race&#39;s welfare cannot support the word &quot;civilization.&quot;</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · strange beasts and foreign races&#39; situation described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./50-万族谱系总览.html">50-Myriad Races Genealogy Overview</a> · <a href="./52-异族分类与共生.html">52-Foreign-Race Classification and Symbiosis</a> · <a href="./53-奇特生命识别标准.html">53-Strange-Life Recognition Standards</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const m=t(s,[["render",o]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
